invariant: INV-16
file: record.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_widemul
reason: the record layer runs every record's Poly1305 on the decomposition
  whatever the session answered, so a caller that stated the multiply's
  timing gets the slow copy on every record and the answer picks nothing
  there. The tags are the same. test/tcp_blocking_loop_widemul.h requires
  a handshake between two ends that answer CH_WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME to
  call no file under its own names.

--- old
    return d->widemul;
--- new
    (void)d;
    return CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED;
